  "story": {
    "day": 163,
    "title": "Kaya's Family Day Out",
    "sentences": [
      "Kaya's family packed a suitcase for hiking.",
      "It was a cloudy morning; they drove forty kilometers.",
      "At the public park, they had to answer a quick question.",
      "She saw a horse, sheep, a zebra, and a pig.",
      "Children played dodge ball near the playground with a rope.",
      "They visited a shop to sell old things for money.",
      "Her mom bought chicken, pork steak, potatoes, spaghetti, and a lemon.",
      "She also picked tomatoes, lettuce, cabbage, corn, and mushrooms.",
      "\"I'll make curry with such good seasoning!\" she said, like a million times.",
      "For dessert, they ate pudding.",
      "Kaya felt tired at 7 p.m. She moved forward.",
      "She wasn't scared of wolves; she remembered skiing, a koala, and calligraphy."
    ]
  }
}